 "blurb": "The picture set in a block of soft gel standing on the bottom of the frame. It answers how the camera really moved: a pan makes the block lean the other way, overshoot and jiggle in two or three ripples at once, a tilt squashes it so it bulges at the sides, and a light catches the bending surface while it wobbles. When the camera settles the block settles too. A still shot stays exactly as it was.",
